# Panko Fish Tacos

Based on [https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/panko-fish-tacos](https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/panko-fish-tacos) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250916131227/https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/panko-fish-tacos))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 454g [white fish of choice]{ ing="white-fish-of-choice" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } (a sprinkle, plus more for finishing)
- [ ] 80g [flour]{ ing="flour" }
- [ ] 40g [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 2 [eggs]{ ing="egg" } (beaten)
- [ ] 100g [panko bread crumbs]{ ing="panko-bread-crumbs" }
- [ ] [Neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } (as needed for frying, or cooking spray for air frying)
- [ ] 1 [lime]{ ing="lime" } (for zest and juice)
- [ ] 6-8 [corn tortillas]{ ing="corn-tortillas" }
- [ ] [Pickled onions]{ ing="pickled-onions" } or red onions (as needed)
- [ ] [Shredded cabbage]{ ing="shredded-cabbage" } or coleslaw mix (optional, for crunch)
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" } (as needed)
- [ ] [Limes]{ ing="limes" } (as needed for serving)

### Sauce options (choose one or mix)

- [ ] [Kewpie mayo]{ ing="kewpie-mayo" }
- [ ] [Chipotle mayo]{ ing="chipotle-mayo" } (mayo + chipotle in adobo)
- [ ] [Sriracha mayo]{ ing="sriracha-mayo" } (mayo + sriracha)
- [ ] [Avocado crema]{ ing="avocado-crema" } (avocado + sour cream/Greek yogurt + lime)
- [ ] [Cilantro lime crema]{ ing="cilantro-lime-crema" } (sour cream/Greek yogurt + cilantro + lime + garlic)
- [ ] [Hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }

## Recipe

1. Remove any bones from the fish and slice into large sticks matching your [tortilla]{ ing="corn-tortillas" } size. Pat fish completely dry with paper towels. Sprinkle [salt]{ ing="salt" } evenly over pieces. Optionally, refrigerate for an hour or overnight.
1. Prepare three trays with [flour]{ ing="flour" }-[cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } mixture, beaten [egg]{ ing="egg" }, and panko [crumbs]{ ing="panko-bread-crumbs" } separately. Coat fish in flour mixture, dip in egg, then roll in panko, pressing gently to adhere.
1. **For deep frying**: Heat [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } (about 2 inches deep) in a wok or dutch oven to 350°F (176°C). Gently place fish in oil and fry in batches for 4-6 minutes total, agitating occasionally. Avoid overcrowding. **For air frying**: Preheat air fryer to 400°F (204°C). Place breaded fish in a single layer in basket, spray lightly with cooking oil. Cook 10-12 minutes without flipping (or flip halfway for extra even browning). Avoid overcrowding.
1. Transfer cooked fish to paper towel-lined rack (if fried) or plate. Sprinkle with [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [lime]{ ing="limes" } zest, and juice. Serve on warm [tortillas]{ ing="corn-tortillas" } with your [choice]{ ing="white-fish-of-choice" } of toppings.

## Notes

- Creator Ethan Chlebowski recommends this tonkatsu-style breading over traditional batter for better texture with fresh toppings
- Cod is suggested as a mild white fish option
- Air frying reduces oil significantly while maintaining crispy panko texture - key is patting fish dry and using cooking spray
- Serves 6-8
- Total time: 45 minutes (deep frying) or 30 minutes (air frying)
